 "completeness": "partial: US and CSUS ages + dose-rate components only for T1-T3 (T4-T8 inputs only, no age computed by authors); side assignment of the two removed thicknesses not stated; gamma and cosmic not printed separately per sample (gamma+cosmic only; text gives cosmic 26.8 µGy/a at 21 m); water basis not stated ('% wgt')",
 "extraction_notes": "Read via WebFetch several times. A first per-sample read mis-aligned the columns (depth/sediment shifted); a raw-text extraction of Table 3 resolved the layout: columns are Initial enamel thickness | Removed thickness ((1) on enamel line, (2) on dentine line) | Depth (m) | Sediment U (ppm) | Th (ppm) | K (%) | DE (Gy). The 21 ± 3 m depth matches the text ('present-day depth (i.e. 21m, leading to a cosmic dose of 26.8 µGy/a)'); sediment U~1.1, Th~4, K~0.7 matches the independent MNHN sediment analyses (Table 4), supporting this alignment. U-series ratios are printed as 234U/238U and 230Th/238U (NOT 230Th/234U); stored under 'th230_u238' (extra key) and th230_u234 left null -- convert if needed (230Th/234U = 230Th/238U / 234U/238U). The (1)/(2) removed thicknesses are stored as removed_side1_um/removed_side2_um because the paper does not say which side is which (presumably (1) outer/sediment side and (2) dentine side, unverified). Dentine water 5 ± 3 %, sediment 20 ± 10 % from Table 1. Ages correspond to original De (Table 3), not the Table 7 recalculated De.",
 "benchmark": true
}